# Trivia Quiz

A modular and scalable **Trivia Quiz web application** built using **HTML, CSS, and modern JavaScript (ES Modules)**.

Originally started as a beginner learning exercise inspired by a quiz concept seen in the **Mimo learning platform**, this project has evolved into a structured frontend application focused on:

- application architecture
- modular design
- state management
- UI flow control
- maintainable folder structure
- scalable quiz logic

The project demonstrates how to build a **real browser application without frameworks**, while still applying professional frontend engineering patterns.

---

# Live Demo

https://blackravenwolf.github.io/trivia-quiz/

---

# Purpose

This project exists as an **advanced learning project** to practice real-world frontend architecture.

Main learning goals:

1. Modular JavaScript architecture (ES Modules)
2. Application state management
3. UI rendering flow separation
4. Scalable quiz logic design
5. Maintainable CSS architecture
6. Debugging and refactoring workflows
7. Preparing for multiplayer and backend integration

---

# Features

## Gameplay

- Large categorized question database
- Difficulty levels:
  - Easy
  - Medium
  - Hard
  - Expert
- Mixed difficulty distribution logic
- Random question selection per quiz
- No duplicate questions within one session
- Answer shuffle system
- Immediate answer validation after selection
- Countdown timer per question
- Real-time score tracking
- Progress indicator and animated score bar

## Screens

- Start Screen
- Options Screen
- Credits Screen
- Quiz Screen
- Final completion state
- Restart quiz functionality
- Return to main menu

## Quiz Settings

- Difficulty selection
- Question amount selection (Quick → Ultimate)
- Multi-category selection
- Live preview of selected settings

## UI / UX

- Glassmorphism quiz card design
- Gradient background image overlay
- Window-style header bar
- Animated timer progress bar
- Smooth feedback transitions
- Fully responsive layout (desktop / tablet / mobile)

---

